I'm gonna take a few minutes today to  tell you about a really exciting  blockchain project that we are  partnering with called silica this is  the second video in a two-part series we  are doing you can learn even more about  silica by going to their website I've  put the link right down underneath the  video  what makes silica such an interesting  project is that it solves a very big and  very real problem that blockchain and  cryptocurrency are facing and it's a  problem that's inhibited the utility and  the adoption of blockchain and that is  the problem of scalability and of course  what I'm talking about here are the  limitations that some of the most  popular block chains have in their  ability to grow as a network and to keep  processing more and more transactions  two well-known examples  Bitcoin and aetherium they have inherent  constraints in their capacity to expand  to scale and this ability to scale is  crucial for many blockchain use cases  especially enterprise use cases so  there's a lot of competition in the  blockchain space to meet that need and  to develop a protocol that can further  scale in order to bridge the gap meet  the demand of businesses and projects  that require it  so Silica's approach to solving this  problem has been to develop a brand new  blockchain protocol where throughput in  other words the network's ability to  process transactions goes up as the  network gets bigger and the way that  they do this is through a mechanism  called a shard each node of the  blockchain network is divided into  shards which are sort of like sub  networks and it's the multiple levels of  this hierarchy which are processing  transactions in parallel that multiply  the total throughput of the network and  allow it to scale in a linear fashion  the more the network grows the more  transactions that it's actually able to  process and zelicah is the first  blockchain platform ever to implement  shards in this way to use shards as a  solution for scaling on a public  blockchain so that is like the crux of  Zillah cos unique offering and what has  allowed it to gain  so much traction in terms of adoption I  talked a little bit about Zil hive in my  previous video I want to fill you in a  little more about that which is really  interesting  Zil hive is a program that silica has  put together to engage with and give  back to the community and it encourages  the development and adoption of apps  built on silica through a pool of five  million dollars in grants that go to  projects teams and individuals that are  building tools and apps with silica and  doing research on the platform and the  grants target entrepreneurs who are  building the most innovative apps that  tokenized real-world assets and enable  the issuance of digital identity enabled  the exchange of goods and services in a  digital marketplace these are three  rapidly emerging use cases for Zillah  cos technologies and ones that they are  doing a lot to try to bolster couple of  cool updates on silica and what they've  been up to since my first video was  published a couple of weeks ago silica  announced the new partnership with a  platform called switch IO to build a  noncustodial decentralized exchange  index and the new silicon decks will  allow silica token holders and traders  to tap into digital assets on the  etherium blockchain for the first time  ever the new decks will have an atomic  swap protocol that will allow traders to  do automatic digital asset exchanges  without needing a centralized  intermediary and users will also be able  to contribute to liquidity pools  allowing for consistent market making  while they get a cut of each transaction  fee number two silica also just issued  their to their community to introduce  staking to the network and this is a  really big deal because it's something  the community has been waiting for since  day one on the main net and they're  going to be building out the staking  over the next few months they'll  incorporate feedback from developers  token holders and miners in the silica  community which is great it's clear  silica is constantly engaging and taking  direction from people who are invested  in the platform and the idea there is  build up the ecosystem in a way that  will benefit everybody involved I've  really enjoyed talking about silica in  these two videos you can check out the  first one I did  I want to thank silica for partnering  and collaborating with us on creating  this content  there are many blockchain projects out  there but this is one that's really  doing something new and useful with  scalability check out silica using the  link underneath this video subscribe to  their newsletter follow them on Twitter  they have a big big following they also  have some really interesting stuff going  on right now definitely a project you'll  want to continue paying attention to in  the future
 

